   "id": "bekhorot.29a.12",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "אִם הָיָה כֹּהֵן מְטַמְּאֵהוּ מִתְּרוּמָתוֹ כּוּ׳. אִיהוּ גּוּפֵיהּ הֵיכִי אָזֵיל?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: Although taking wages is prohibited, «if» the one examining the firstborn, or the judge, or the witness, «was a priest,» and the one who required his services «rendered him impure» and prevented him «from» partaking of «his teruma,» he must provide the priest with food, drink, and oil. The Gemara asks: But «he himself,» the priest, «how» was he permitted to «go» to a place that caused him to become impure? It is prohibited for a priest to render himself ritually impure."
  }
 ],
